{"id":1634,"date":"2020-12-04T11:19:00","date_gmt":"2020-12-04T19:19:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1634"},"modified":"2024-08-27T13:04:47","modified_gmt":"2024-08-27T20:04:47","slug":"codrone-blockly-sr-flight-directions","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-sr-flight-directions\/","title":{"rendered":"Flight Directions"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221552da847\" name=\"6a221552da847\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight movements<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Air vehicles move a little differently than land vehicles. While land vehicles can move forward, backward, and sometimes side-to-side, air vehicles can do all of that and move up and down. To keep track of how a CoDrone moves in a three-dimensional space, you can use the terms below:<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Roll <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">controls the CoDrone&#8217;s horizontal, or side to side, movement. Positive roll will make the CoDrone move to the right, and negative roll will make the drone move to the left. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;955&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<b>Pitch <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">is the CoDrone&#8217;s forward and backward tilt. Positive pitch will make the CoDrone tilt and move forward, and negative pitch will make the CoDrone tilt and move backwards. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;958&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<b>Yaw <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">is the CoDrone&#8217;s left and right rotation. Positive yaw will make the CoDrone turn to the right, and negative yaw will make the CoDrone turn to the left.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;959&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<b>Throttle <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">controls the CoDrone&#8217;s vertical, or up and down, movement. Positive throttle will make the CoDrone fly higher, and negative throttle will make the CoDrone fly lower.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;960&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Be careful with yaw and roll! Yaw will make your CoDrone turn left or right, while roll will move your CoDrone left or right.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221552dab83\" name=\"6a221552dab83\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Blind drone<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Have a friend sit down, blindfold them (or just have them keep their eyes closed), and guide them through an obstacle course to sitting down in a different chair using only flight movement words. Make sure that anything dangerous is out of their way first!\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Positive throttle: stand up\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Negative throttle: sit down\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Positive pitch: move forward\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Negative pitch: move backward\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Positive yaw: turn right\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Negative yaw: turn left\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Positive roll: move right\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Negative roll: turn left\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For example, if you wanted to tell your friend to move forward, you could say, &#8220;Positive pitch 2 steps.&#8221; That would let your friend know that you want them to move forward by 2 steps. Once your friend successfully completes the obstacle course, switch roles so they can give you directions!\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221552dad2b\" name=\"6a221552dad2b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Move<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">There is one block in Blockly that will help you program your CoDrone to fly in any of the flight directions! You can find the move block in the flight commands menu in Blockly. Once you drag it to your workspace, you can fill in the number of seconds you would like your CoDrone to move for. <\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1635&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each flight direction has a percent symbol next to it, and that is for the power value. T<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">hese values can range<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">from -100 to 100, with 0 being no movement in that direction and -100 or 100 being full speed. For example,<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">if you have your throttle set at -78, your CoDrone will move downwards at 78% speed. In general, if you want<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">your CoDrone to move to the right, forwards, or up, you should use positive numbers. If you want your<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone to move to the left, backwards, or down, you should use negative numbers.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1636&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">With this block, you can also have your CoDrone move in more than one direction at a time! All you need to<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">do is type in values for each direction you would like your CoDrone to move in. For example, if you want your<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone to move diagonally to the right, you would type in positive values for both pitch and roll while<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">leaving throttle and yaw alone.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">One problem: once you type in your numbers, the names of the flight directions will disappear from the block!<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To remember the order they appear in (<\/span><b>R<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">oll, <\/span><b>P<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">itch, <\/span><b>Y<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">aw, and <\/span><b>T<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">hrottle), use the mnemonic device <\/span><b>R<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">obots <\/span><b>P<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">lay<\/span> <b>Y<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">ellow <\/span><b>T<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">rombones.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221552dadc7\" name=\"6a221552dadc7\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Turn<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In addition to being able to fly up, down, left, right, forward, and backward, your CoDrone can also turn left<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">and right! The turn block in the flight commands menu can help you program your CoDrone to do<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">this. Note: you can also use yaw in your move block!<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1637&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To use the turn() block, drag it to your workspace and select left or right from the drop-down menu. Type in the number of seconds you would like your CoDrone to turn for, and then type in the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">power value. This number can range from 0 to 100, with 0 being completely still and 100 being very fast. We<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">recommend starting at 50 and seeing what you need to do from there.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221552dae29\" name=\"6a221552dae29\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Flight variables<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can also use the blocks in the aqua flight variables menu to move your drone. These blocks work exactly the same way as the blue move block, but they&#8217;re more broken down. You can stack blocks to make your CoDrone to go in one or a couple of directions at once (like diagonally to the right), and then use the aqua move block afterwards.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1639&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try the code below to see what happens!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1640&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Warning: if you want to see distinct directions one after the other, you will need to set the previously flown direction back to 0% before adding on the new flight direction. Otherwise, your drone will keep performing that action throughout the entire program. Try the program below after testing out the program above to see what we mean.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1641&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221552dae73\" name=\"6a221552dae73\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Put it all together!<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Try writing a program that will have your CoDrone take off, fly forward, and then turn before landing!\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1638&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221552db012\" name=\"6a221552db012\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Shapeshifter<\/b><b>\u00a0<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Have your CoDrone fly in a shape using all of the commands you just learned! The only rule is that you HAVE<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to include a kill switch.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Some helpful hints:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A triangle\u2019s angles add up to 180 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A quadrilateral\u2019s angles add up to 360 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A pentagon\u2019s angles add up to 540 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A hexagon\u2019s angles add up to 720 degrees.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">An octagon\u2019s angles add up to 1080 degrees.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Flight movements [vc_column_text]Air vehicles move a little differently than land vehicles. While land vehicles can move forward, backward, and sometimes side-to-side, air vehicles can do all of&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-sr-flight-directions\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1753,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":806,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,144,167,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,2164,2115,2122,2126],"class_list":["post-1634","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-flight-directions","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","module-senior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1634","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":6,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1634\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12723,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1634\/revisions\/12723"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1753"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1634"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1634"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1634"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}